-- title:
--   Vanishing germ of the half-weighted orbital integral at non-norm parameters
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L/K$ finite and Galois, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic with generator $\sigma$), and assume $[L:K]$ is prime. Let $v$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, with completion $K_v$ and integers $\mathcal{O}_v$. Let $\varphi : \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v) \to \mathbb{C}$ be locally constant with compact support, let $f : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) \to \mathbb{C}$ be locally constant with compact support, and assume $\varphi$ and $f$ satisfy the matching relation `AreMatchingOn` for $\sigma$ with respect to the semi-local and local Haar measures `semiLocalHaar` and `localHaar`. Let $\mu$ be an additive Haar measure on $K_v$, for the Borel structure, normalised by $\mu(\mathcal{O}_v) = 1$. Then, $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ being given its Borel structure, there are a function $\Lambda_0 : K_v^\times \to \mathbb{C}$, a constant $C_0 \in \mathbb{R}$ and a neighbourhood $U$ of $1$ in $K_v^\times$ such that for every $a \in K_v^\times$ which is not the $K_v$-algebra norm of any unit of $L \otimes_K K_v$, and every $t \in U$ with $t \neq 1$,
--   $$\bigl\| 2[L:K]\,H(a, at) - \Lambda_0(a) \bigr\| \le C_0\,\|1 - t\|\,\bigl(1 + |\log\|1-t\||\bigr),$$
--   where $H(a,b)$ is the half-weighted orbital quantity
--   $$H(a,b) = -\sqrt{\tfrac{\|a\|}{\|b\|}} \int_{\{x \in K_v\,:\,\|1 - ba^{-1}\| < \|x\|\}} \Bigl(\int_{\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathcal{O}_v)} f(\mathrm{arg}\,k\,a\,b\,x)\,d\,\mathrm{localHaar}(k)\Bigr)\bigl(\log\|x\| - \log\|1 - ba^{-1}\|\bigr)\,d\mu(x),$$
--   the inner integral being over the set of $k \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ with both $k$ and $k^{-1}$ having entries in $\mathcal{O}_v$, against `localHaar` restricted to that set. The constant $C_0$ and the neighbourhood $U$ are uniform in $a$.
--
--   This is the local germ estimate at the central point for parameters $a$ outside the norms from $(L \otimes_K K_v)^\times$: for such $a$ the half-weighted orbital integral of a matching test function, multiplied by $2[L:K]$, differs from a function of $a$ alone by $O(\|1-t\|(1+|\log\|1-t\||))$ as $t \to 1$, so that both singular coefficients of the germ expansion drop out. It feeds the comparison of twisted and standard weighted orbital integrals used in the cyclic base change argument for $\mathrm{GL}_2$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_forall_norm_halfWeighted_sub_le_of_not_exists_norm_eq_of_areMatchingLocal.lean

